 ## Batch 3 — GX depth and alpha state families
 
-An actual Z24 seed/interpolation/comparison/readback probe is implemented. Direct interpolation fails near ties; canonical source-Z input passes 48 GPU cases including deferred CT32 alpha. The bounded ledger and auxiliary ownership boundaries are implemented; registering the resident depth engine in the runtime is still open. See [GX-Z24-EXPERIMENT.md](GX-Z24-EXPERIMENT.md) and [GX-Z24-INTEGRATION.md](GX-Z24-INTEGRATION.md).
+An actual Z24 seed/interpolation/comparison/readback probe is implemented. Direct interpolation fails near ties; canonical source-Z input passes 48 GPU cases including deferred CT32 alpha. The bounded ledger and auxiliary ownership boundaries are implemented; the resident depth engine is registered in the GX driver behind `PS2X_WII_GX_DEPTH24` (default OFF; private Wii build ON) for opaque untextured Z24 GEQUAL+write draws. Actual game speed is not yet measured. See [GX-Z24-EXPERIMENT.md](GX-Z24-EXPERIMENT.md) and [GX-Z24-INTEGRATION.md](GX-Z24-INTEGRATION.md).
 
 - [ ] Measure actual GS depth/alpha/blend families in title and gameplay captures. Startup measured: Z24, GEQUAL with depth writes; most sampled triangles have unconditional alpha. Title/gameplay capture remains open.
 - [ ] Define depth encoding and precision limits (GS Z32/Z24/Z16 versus GX Z24).
