--- orig/PS2Recomp/docs/wii/GX-Z24-INTEGRATION.md	2026-10-29 15:25:06.000000000 +0000
+++ src/PS2Recomp/docs/wii/GX-Z24-INTEGRATION.md	2026-10-29 20:57:27.317221015 +0000
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
 
 The generated GX adapter has drain-only auxiliary owner registration, a resolve callback before RGB/alpha import, and a read-only source-disjoint callback. It rejects owner changes while GPU work is pending and treats resolve failure as terminal. Connected GPU tests verify ordering before old VRAM is overwritten, mixed CPU/GX transitions and auxiliary source aliases in compact and full staging modes.
 
-`GSNativeDrawDriver::NeedsResolveBeforeSubmit` lets the coordinator materialize a pending auxiliary owner before a different native path reads CPU metadata. Host tests verify that this preserves native routing and that query failures remain terminal. No depth engine is registered by the current game runtime yet.
+`GSNativeDrawDriver::NeedsResolveBeforeSubmit` lets the coordinator materialize a pending auxiliary owner before a different native path reads CPU metadata. Host tests verify that this preserves native routing and that query failures remain terminal. With `PS2X_WII_GX_DEPTH24` the driver registers `ps2_wii_gx_depth24_engine.h` (128 KiB upload arena, seed bitmap, resident Z24 ownership, deferred exact CT32 alpha replay, Z copyback before RGB import). Eligibility is opaque untextured triangles with Z24 GEQUAL and depth write over disjoint frame/Z envelopes; everything else resolves and takes the previous path. Canonical source depth is still computed on the CPU. Connected host/Dolphin probe: 346/346 with exact structural VRAM and bounded RGB error. The 347-case mixed sequence (fog fallback, explicit Z read, texture flush, ledger-cap transition, arena wrap) builds but its Dolphin run and any actual game run are pending; no speed or MEM2-headroom claim exists yet.
 
